card.statement:
There exists a unique surjective $\A$-algebra homomorphism $\phi_d^\imath: \Ki \rightarrow \Si$ such that

for $R \ge 0$, $i \in [1,n-1]$ and $D \in {}^\imath \txid$,

\begin{align*}
\phi_d^\imath ( [D+ R E^{\theta}_{n,n+2}]) &=
\begin{cases}
[D+ R E^{\theta}_{n,n+2}], &\text{ if } D+ R E^{\theta}_{n,n+2} \in {}^\imath \Xi_d;\\
0, &\text{ otherwise; }
\end{cases}\\
\phi_d^\imath ( [D+ R E^{\theta}_{i,i+1}]) &=
\begin{cases}[D+ R E^{\theta}_{i,i+1}], &\text{ if } D+ R E^{\theta}_{i,i+1} \in {}^\imath \Xi_d;\\
0, &\text{ otherwise; }
\end{cases}\\
\phi_d^\imath ( [D+ R E^{\theta}_{i+1,i}]) &=
\begin{cases}
[D+ R E^{\theta}_{i+1,i}], &\text{ if } D+ R E^{\theta}_{i+1,i} \in {}^\imath \Xi_d;\\
0, &\text{ otherwise. }
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
